title: '[asset-hub-westend] XCM fee benchmarks on the swap trader'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: "Asset Hub Westend's `pallet_xcm_benchmarks::generic` worst case for\
    \ `BuyExecution`, `PayFees` and `RefundSurplus` pays fees in WND. That path is\
    \ `UsingComponents`, which never touches the pool. Fees paid in any other asset\
    \ go through `SwapFirstAssetTrader`, which swaps against `pallet_asset_conversion`,\
    \ and the runtime charges the WND weight for it. Locally that is about 28 \xB5\
    s charged for about 120 \xB5s of work.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `worst_case_for_trader`\
    \ pays in a foreign asset with a pool against WND, so the swap is what gets measured.\
    \ The pool setup is shared with `worst_case_asset_exchange`, which already created\
    \ the same asset and pool inline. `worst_case_holding` gains that asset so the\
    \ holding register can pay with it.\n- `refund_surplus` buys twice the surplus\
    \ it refunds. `SwapFirstAssetTrader` refunds nothing when the refund would be the\
    \ whole fee it holds, so with purchase equal to surplus the refund was zero and the\
    \ benchmark's assertion failed against it.\n\n## Origin\n\nSplit out of #12581 at reviewer\
    \ request, since the under-benchmarked swap exists on master independently of\
    \ that PR and should be reviewable and backportable on its own."
- audience: Runtime User
  description: |-
    Asset Hub Westend charges `BuyExecution`, `PayFees` and `RefundSurplus` the weight of the
    swap path whatever the fee asset, so messages paying in WND are charged more as well:
    `buy_execution` about 9 times, `pay_fees` about 3 times and `refund_surplus` about 115 times
    the previous weight. Senders with a hard-coded `Limited` weight limit covering these
    instructions may now fail with `Overweight` and should raise it.
crates:
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-xcm-benchmarks
  bump: patch
